              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "परिवार (parivār) — \"family\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Sanskrit, and it comes apart in the hand: pari-, 'around', on the root vṛ, 'to cover, to enclose'. Your family, in this word, is what surrounds you. The same root gives आवरण (āvaraṇ), 'a covering' — one root, two very different everyday words."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Three of four, and a word you can take apart rather than memorise."
            }
          ]
        },
