        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: लोग",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "लोग (log) — \"people\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "From Sanskrit लोक (loka), 'world, realm': the word for the world slid across to mean the people in it. Latin lucus, a clearing in a forest, and lux, 'light', grow from the same ancient root — an open, lit space first, then whoever stands in it. Hindi hears लोग (log) as already plural, so it needs no further ending."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "That closes the run: son, daughter, family, and everyone else."
            }
          ]
        },
